== arc42/arc42  path knowledge/arc42.md  rev 2730a468c51c
Lens direction [## Building Block View]: Which way the arrows point (unreviewed)
  Read the diagram as a stranger would: can they tell what depends on what, and what
  would break in which direction? A box-and-line picture with no direction is a
  seating chart. Check it against the `depends_on` edges — where the prose and the
  graph disagree, one of them is out of date.
Lens deferred [## Deferred Decisions]: Deferred, with a reason it can wait (unreviewed)
  Each deferred item should say what would force it back onto the table. "Later"
  without a trigger is how a spine quietly rots — nobody ever notices the moment it
  stopped being safe to wait.
----- BEGIN arc42/arc42 rev 2730a468c51c -----
## Introduction and Goals

<!-- what this system is for, and the one or two decisions that matter most -->

## Architecture Constraints

<!-- forces from outside the design space - platform, budget, org boundary, compliance -->

## Context and Scope

<!-- the system boundary - the systems and people outside it, named, and what crosses the line -->

## Solution Strategy

<!-- the shape and why - one paragraph per big call, each stating the choice and its cost; a pinned stack, with versions, earns a table here -->

## Building Block View

<!-- each part by name and what it owns, one line each; the diagram below carries the direction -->

## Runtime View

<!-- only the interactions a quality target stresses - a numbered walk or a sequence, at component altitude -->

## Deployment View

<!-- the runtime nodes and environments, and the structural reason they are separate -->

## Crosscutting Concepts

<!-- auth, errors, logging, config, naming - the rules that hold everywhere; the domain data model belongs here too, as an ERD -->

## Architecture Decisions

<!-- one line per decision - what was chosen and why it still holds; full records in knowledge/decisions/ -->

## Quality Requirements

<!-- the measurable targets - a number, a unit, and the point it is measured at -->

## Risks and Technical Debt

## Glossary

<!-- the ubiquitous language - term, one line each -->

## Deferred Decisions

<!-- decisions pushed down on purpose, each with the event that reopens it -->

## Open Questions

<!-- what only a human can settle, each with who answers it and what it blocks -->

## Assumptions Index

<!-- every assumption this record proceeds on, and the consequence if it is wrong -->

## Grounding Evidence

<!-- the audit appendix - what was read to write this, and when -->
